 ## Shared principles
-Builds on the [Shared principles](11-producing-volume-data.md) of the parent family. All methods map a conceptual or physical source into a discrete or analytic volumetric representation suitable for rendering [G]. The core mechanism involves:
-1. **Domain Definition**: Establishing a spatial domain, typically a 3D grid with resolution $(N_x, N_y, N_z)$ and bounding box, or an infinite analytic space [G].
-2. **Value Assignment**: Determining the value (density, distance, color) for each point in the domain based on the source method (geometric intersection, function evaluation, or physical state) [G].
-3. **Storage/Access**: Either storing the result in a discrete array (voxelization, simulation) or providing an interface to compute it on-the-fly (procedural) [G].
+Builds on the [Shared principles](11-producing-volume-data.md) of the parent family [G].
 
 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Position Based Fluids](1765-position-based-fluids.md)
-A Lagrangian particle-based fluid simulation method that enforces incompressibility by directly correcting particle positions to satisfy density constraints. It differs from pressure-based solvers by using constraint projection within a Position-Based Dynamics framework, which stabilizes the simulation and avoids density drift. It builds on [Simulation output](15-simulation-output.md) and is distinct from [Gaussian Splashing](1387-gaussian-splashing.md) and [Smoke Advection](4639-smoke-advection.md) by decoupling simulation from rendering and operating entirely in particle space. Choose this when real-time, incompressible fluid behavior is required without the stability issues of pressure-based solvers.
