 ### Fire Reaction Coordinate
-Tracks a reaction coordinate to simulate fire, which indicates time since ignition and fuel exhaustion [S2, unofficial]. The reaction coordinate $Y$ evolves as $\frac{\partial Y}{\partial t} = -(u \cdot \nabla) Y - k$, where $u$ is velocity and $k$ is a constant decrement per time step [S2, unofficial]. A value of 1 indicates just-ignited gas, and a value < 0 indicates fuel exhaustion [S2, unofficial]. It differs from simple density fields by explicitly modeling the fuel consumption process. Choose this when realistic fire behavior (ignition, burning, extinction) is needed.
