 ### Massless Particle System
-Particles are used as tracer elements to visualize flow, as droplets to model fire suppression, or as fuel elements (embers) [S3, unofficial]. Positions are determined by a differential equation assuming drag force is large compared to gravity [S3, unofficial]. Particle positions are determined using $\frac{dx_p}{dt} = V(x_p, t)$, where $x_p$ is particle position and $V$ is velocity [S3, unofficial]. It differs from dense particle fluids by treating particles as passive tracers or sparse embers rather than a continuous medium. Choose this for visualizing flow paths or sparse particulate effects like embers.
