 ## Background
-Simulation-based volume generation has its roots in computational fluid dynamics (CFD) and computer graphics research from the 1980s and 1990s. Jos Stam's stable fluids [G] laid the groundwork for Eulerian grid-based smoke simulation. The integration of fire dynamics with reaction coordinates was popularized by Nguyen et al. (2002) in the context of GPU-based fluid simulation [S2, unofficial]. Massless particle systems have been used in fire safety visualization tools like Smokeview, developed by NIST, for decades [S3, unofficial]. These methods are widely used in visual effects, scientific visualization, and real-time game engines.
